ntain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"\nvalues."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this when the schema represents the final valid shape but the UI needs\nintermediate empty states, such as an unselected date. Raw form state\nremains available as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":"; read each validator's parsed output from the\ncorresponding "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs"},{"type":"text","value":" entry during submission."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the schema as the first argument and the options as the second.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" infer an editable form shape constrained by the schema\ninput, and callbacks receive that shape merged with the schema input. The\nfirst argument is ignored at runtime; include the schema in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwhen it should run."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"remarks-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remarks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". Optional properties such\nas "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators"},{"type":"text","value":" therefore remain optional even when supplied. This\ntradeoff enables safer inference and reuse."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const bookingSchema = z.object({ startDate: z.date() })\nconst bookingOptions = formOptions.looseSchema(bookingSchema, {\n  defaultValues: { startDate: null },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['blur'],\n      run: bookingSchema,\n    },\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.startDate === null ? 'Choose a date' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n  onSubmit: ({ schemaOutputs }) => saveBooking(schemaOutputs[0]),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The original options object, normalized to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" with\nomitted, nullable, and undefined editable states merged into the schema's\ninput shape."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"type-param","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Param"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSchema"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library-managed. Do not specify explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"type-param-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Param"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFormValidators"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library-managed. Do not specify explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"type-param-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Param"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFormData"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library-managed. Do not specify explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"type-param-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Param"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSubmitReturn"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library-managed. Do not specify explicitly."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"strictschema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"strictSchema"}]},{"type":"code","value":"strictSchema: FormOptionsStrictSchemaFn<TComponents>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L280","children":[{"type":"text","value":"utils.public.ts:280"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Infers the form data type from a Standard Schema validator and requires\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" to match the schema input."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this when the schema represents an input-to-output pipeline. Raw form\nstate remains available as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":"; read each validator's parsed output\nfrom the corresponding "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs"},{"type":"text","value":" entry during submission."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the schema as the first argument and the options as the second. This\nfixes the form data to the schema input before the options are inferred, so\neach callback receives a typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":". The first argument is ignored at\nruntime; include the schema in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators"},{"type":"text","value":" when it should run."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"remarks-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remarks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". Optional properties such\nas "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators"},{"type":"text","value":" therefore remain optional even when supplied. This\ntradeoff enables safer inference and reuse."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const profileSchema = z.object({ name: z.string().min(1) })\nconst profileOptions = formOptions.strictSchema(profileSchema, {\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: profileSchema,\n    },\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.name.length === 0 ? 'Name is required' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n  onSubmit: ({ schemaOutputs }) => saveProfile(schemaOutputs[0]),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The original options object, normalized to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" with the\nschema's input shape."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"type-param-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Param"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSchema"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library-managed. Do not specify explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"type-param-6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Param"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFormValidators"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library-managed. Do not specify explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"type-param-7","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Param"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFormData"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library-managed. Do not specify explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"type-param-8","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Param"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSubmitReturn"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Library-managed. Do not specify explicitly."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tcomponents","text":"TComponents","level":3},{"id":"type-parameters-2","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tformdata","text":"TFormData","level":3},{"id":"tformvalidators","text":"TFormValidators","level":3},{"id":"tsubmitreturn","text":"TSubmitReturn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"remarks","text":"Remarks","level":2},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"looseschema","text":"looseSchema","level":3},{"id":"remarks-2","text":"Remarks","level":4},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"type-param","text":"Type Param","level":4},{"id":"type-param-2","text":"Type Param","level":4},{"id":"type-param-3","text":"Type Param","level":4},{"id":"type-param-4","text":"Type Param","level":4},{"id":"strictschema","text":"strictSchema","level":3},{"id":"remarks-3","text":"Remarks","level":4},{"id":"example-2","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"returns-3","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"type-param-5","text":"Type Param","level":4},{"id":"type-param-6","text":"Type Param","level":4},{"id":"type-param-7","text":"Type Param","level":4},{"id":"type-param-8","text":"Type Param","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:205](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L205)\n\nThe callable API exposed by `formOptions`, including its schema-driven\ninference modes.\n\nUse `formOptions` directly instead of naming this interface in application\ncode.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TComponents\n\n`TComponents`\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n```ts\nFormOptionsApi<TFormData, TFormValidators, TSubmitReturn>(options): FormOptions<TFormData, TFormValidators, TSubmitReturn, TComponents>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:226](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L226)\n\nKeeps types inferred from `defaultValues`, validators, and submission\ncallbacks when form options are declared separately.\n\n`defaultValues` determine the form data shape in this mode. At runtime,\nthis returns the original options object and does not create a form or run\nvalidation.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFormData\n\n`TFormData`\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n### TFormValidators\n\n`TFormValidators` *extends* [`FormValidators`](../type-aliases/FormValidators.md)\\<`TFormData`\\>\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n### TSubmitReturn\n\n`TSubmitReturn`\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n[`FormOptions`](FormOptions.md)\\<`TFormData`, `TFormValidators`, `TSubmitReturn`, `unknown`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n[`FormOptions`](FormOptions.md)\\<`TFormData`, `TFormValidators`, `TSubmitReturn`, `TComponents`\\>\n\nThe original options object, normalized to `FormOptions` with its\ninferred form data, validator, and submission types.\n\n## Remarks\n\n**Important:** Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to `FormOptions`. Optional properties such\nas `validators` therefore remain optional even when supplied. This\ntradeoff enables safer inference and reuse.\n\n## Properties\n\n### looseSchema\n\n```ts\nlooseSchema: FormOptionsLooseSchemaFn<TComponents>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:332](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L332)\n\nInfers the form data shape from a Standard Schema validator while allowing\neditable defaults to omit properties or contain `null` or `undefined`\nvalues.\n\nUse this when the schema represents the final valid shape but the UI needs\nintermediate empty states, such as an unselected date. Raw form state\nremains available as `value`; read each validator's parsed output from the\ncorresponding `schemaOutputs` entry during submission.\n\nPass the schema as the first argument and the options as the second.\n`defaultValues` infer an editable form shape constrained by the schema\ninput, and callbacks receive that shape merged with the schema input. The\nfirst argument is ignored at runtime; include the schema in `validators`\nwhen it should run.\n\n#### Remarks\n\n**Important:** Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to `FormOptions`. Optional properties such\nas `validators` therefore remain optional even when supplied. This\ntradeoff enables safer inference and reuse.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst bookingSchema = z.object({ startDate: z.date() })\nconst bookingOptions = formOptions.looseSchema(bookingSchema, {\n  defaultValues: { startDate: null },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['blur'],\n      run: bookingSchema,\n    },\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.startDate === null ? 'Choose a date' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n  onSubmit: ({ schemaOutputs }) => saveBooking(schemaOutputs[0]),\n})\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\nThe original options object, normalized to `FormOptions` with\nomitted, nullable, and undefined editable states merged into the schema's\ninput shape.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TSchema**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TFormValidators**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TFormData**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TSubmitReturn**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n***\n\n### strictSchema\n\n```ts\nstrictSchema: FormOptionsStrictSchemaFn<TComponents>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:280](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L280)\n\nInfers the form data type from a Standard Schema validator and requires\n`defaultValues` to match the schema input.\n\nUse this when the schema represents an input-to-output pipeline. Raw form\nstate remains available as `value`; read each validator's parsed output\nfrom the corresponding `schemaOutputs` entry during submission.\n\nPass the schema as the first argument and the options as the second. This\nfixes the form data to the schema input before the options are inferred, so\neach callback receives a typed `value`. The first argument is ignored at\nruntime; include the schema in `validators` when it should run.\n\n#### Remarks\n\n**Important:** Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to `FormOptions`. Optional properties such\nas `validators` therefore remain optional even when supplied. This\ntradeoff enables safer inference and reuse.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst profileSchema = z.object({ name: z.string().min(1) })\nconst profileOptions = formOptions.strictSchema(profileSchema, {\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: profileSchema,\n    },\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.name.length === 0 ? 'Name is required' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n  onSubmit: ({ schemaOutputs }) => saveProfile(schemaOutputs[0]),\n})\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\nThe original options object, normalized to `FormOptions` with the\nschema's input shape.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TSchema**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TFormValidators**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TFormData**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TSubmitReturn**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: FormOptionsApi\ntitle: FormOptionsApi\n---\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:205](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L205)\n\nThe callable API exposed by `formOptions`, including its schema-driven\ninference modes.\n\nUse `formOptions` directly instead of naming this interface in application\ncode.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TComponents\n\n`TComponents`\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n```ts\nFormOptionsApi<TFormData, TFormValidators, TSubmitReturn>(options): FormOptions<TFormData, TFormValidators, TSubmitReturn, TComponents>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:226](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L226)\n\nKeeps types inferred from `defaultValues`, validators, and submission\ncallbacks when form options are declared separately.\n\n`defaultValues` determine the form data shape in this mode. At runtime,\nthis returns the original options object and does not create a form or run\nvalidation.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFormData\n\n`TFormData`\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n### TFormValidators\n\n`TFormValidators` *extends* [`FormValidators`](../type-aliases/FormValidators.md)\\<`TFormData`\\>\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n### TSubmitReturn\n\n`TSubmitReturn`\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n[`FormOptions`](FormOptions.md)\\<`TFormData`, `TFormValidators`, `TSubmitReturn`, `unknown`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n[`FormOptions`](FormOptions.md)\\<`TFormData`, `TFormValidators`, `TSubmitReturn`, `TComponents`\\>\n\nThe original options object, normalized to `FormOptions` with its\ninferred form data, validator, and submission types.\n\n## Remarks\n\n**Important:** Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to `FormOptions`. Optional properties such\nas `validators` therefore remain optional even when supplied. This\ntradeoff enables safer inference and reuse.\n\n## Properties\n\n### looseSchema\n\n```ts\nlooseSchema: FormOptionsLooseSchemaFn<TComponents>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:332](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L332)\n\nInfers the form data shape from a Standard Schema validator while allowing\neditable defaults to omit properties or contain `null` or `undefined`\nvalues.\n\nUse this when the schema represents the final valid shape but the UI needs\nintermediate empty states, such as an unselected date. Raw form state\nremains available as `value`; read each validator's parsed output from the\ncorresponding `schemaOutputs` entry during submission.\n\nPass the schema as the first argument and the options as the second.\n`defaultValues` infer an editable form shape constrained by the schema\ninput, and callbacks receive that shape merged with the schema input. The\nfirst argument is ignored at runtime; include the schema in `validators`\nwhen it should run.\n\n#### Remarks\n\n**Important:** Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to `FormOptions`. Optional properties such\nas `validators` therefore remain optional even when supplied. This\ntradeoff enables safer inference and reuse.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst bookingSchema = z.object({ startDate: z.date() })\nconst bookingOptions = formOptions.looseSchema(bookingSchema, {\n  defaultValues: { startDate: null },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['blur'],\n      run: bookingSchema,\n    },\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.startDate === null ? 'Choose a date' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n  onSubmit: ({ schemaOutputs }) => saveBooking(schemaOutputs[0]),\n})\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\nThe original options object, normalized to `FormOptions` with\nomitted, nullable, and undefined editable states merged into the schema's\ninput shape.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TSchema**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TFormValidators**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TFormData**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TSubmitReturn**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n***\n\n### strictSchema\n\n```ts\nstrictSchema: FormOptionsStrictSchemaFn<TComponents>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:280](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L280)\n\nInfers the form data type from a Standard Schema validator and requires\n`defaultValues` to match the schema input.\n\nUse this when the schema represents an input-to-output pipeline. Raw form\nstate remains available as `value`; read each validator's parsed output\nfrom the corresponding `schemaOutputs` entry during submission.\n\nPass the schema as the first argument and the options as the second. This\nfixes the form data to the schema input before the options are inferred, so\neach callback receives a typed `value`. The first argument is ignored at\nruntime; include the schema in `validators` when it should run.\n\n#### Remarks\n\n**Important:** Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to `FormOptions`. Optional properties such\nas `validators` therefore remain optional even when supplied. This\ntradeoff enables safer inference and reuse.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst profileSchema = z.object({ name: z.string().min(1) })\nconst profileOptions = formOptions.strictSchema(profileSchema, {\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: profileSchema,\n    },\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.name.length === 0 ? 'Name is required' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n  onSubmit: ({ schemaOutputs }) => saveProfile(schemaOutputs[0]),\n})\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\nThe original options object, normalized to `FormOptions` with the\nschema's input shape.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TSchema**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TFormValidators**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TFormData**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n\n#### Type Param\n\n**TSubmitReturn**\n\nLibrary-managed. Do not specify explicitly.\n"}
